  "notes": "Most commonly used for reporting incidents to the police or emergency services.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {警察|けいさつ}に{通報|つうほう}する (report to the police)\n- {消防|しょうぼう}に{通報|つうほう}する (report to the fire department)\n- {匿名|とくめい}で{通報|つうほう}する (report anonymously)\n- {通報|つうほう}を{受|う}ける (receive a report)\n- {通報|つうほう}{者|しゃ} (the person who reported)\n\nIn Japan, 110 is the police emergency number and 119 is fire/ambulance. The phrase 110{番|ばん}{通報|つうほう} specifically means calling the police emergency line.",
